{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/778315-why-do-ghost-wolves-get-the-shaft-so-hard","id":778315,"title":"Why do Ghost Wolves get the shaft so hard?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-02T07:50:15-08:00","id":778315,"title":"Why do Ghost Wolves get the shaft so hard?","content":"To an extent, I get it. This is a game about being part of a pack, a larger community, and they want to encourage you to be part of that. But if you give me the option not to join a tribe, I'd at least like it to be a viable option. Especially when the book makes a point of saying that just because a guy doesn't join a tribe doesn't mean he's abandoned his duties or doesn't want to be part of the Uratha.<br /> <br /> Ghost Wolves get one less dot of renown than everyone else. They get one less gift. They can't start with the second dot of their moon gift. And for all of this they get... nothing. There's no trade-off. There's no benefit to it. If someone sees Ghost Wolves in the book and decides &quot;That sounds kind of cool, I'd like to try that&quot; then the book essentially slaps them in the face for seeing an option it presents them with an liking it.<br /> <br /> I get that werewolves join tribes for a reason. I get that in a game about being part of something larger than yourself, the guy who's standing off on his own is going to be missing out on something. But when you give me an option to play something in a game, I shouldn't just be punished for picking it.<br /> <br /> For contrast, in Masquerade, if you decided you wanted to play a Caitiff, there were some serious consequences to that, but there were a few fringe benefits. All your disciplines cost the same xp, more than an in-clan discipline, but less than for out-of clan, so you could play around with it. You didn't have a clan weakness, outside of being ostracized in vampire society. It was honestly not as good an option as picking a clan, but you got a few trade-offs for choosing the harder road.<br /> <br /> In Forsaken, you get the shaft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T08:06:23-08:00","id":778329,"title":"","content":"I suppose there's two different answers to this.<br /> <br /> The first is that in general in New World of Darkness games, not joining up is always presented as the worst possible option one can take. Being an unbound vampire or apostate mage is just as bad (and from the 2e spoilers, being a courtless changeling is practically a deathwish). As for why this is, one might make some guesses at some of the greater themes of NWoD, that the political game is one worth playing, the benefit of freedom is the freedom itself, etc.<br /> <br /> The second is that (and the Werewolf book isn't fully upfront with this) Tribal Bans are meant to be a huge deal to the Forsaken, and the big perk of being a Ghost Wolf is that you don't have to make a soul-binding oath to one of the Firstborn. You don't have to worry about paying each spirit in kind or honoring your territory in all things or such. Less chance of people banging down your door in the middle of the night as well, most likely. It's not much, but it's something. Maybe Secrets of the Tribes will have some fun stuff for Ghost Wolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T08:17:26-08:00","id":778333,"title":"","content":"A ghost wolf is <i>literally</i> just &quot;werewolf with no tribe.&quot; What they did is take your standard werewolf character generation, looked at the bit where you add tribe, and then just skipped it. You could then join a tribe in-game, and the renown and gift could just slot into place seamlessly, as if you started like that. I wouldn't charge for them if a player did this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T08:21:37-08:00","id":778334,"title":"","content":"It's like asking: Why do newly changed werewolves get the shaft? They start with 9 Harmony and get less renown, so unfair.<br /> <br /> It's because that's what they are. A ghost wolf is a wolf without the benefits of a tribe. Why would there be a tradeoff? The literal only difference is that you don't have a tribe. Tribes give you stuff. If you don't like that, why are you playing a Ghost Wolf?<br /> <br /> For a player's sake though you can just give the guy 3 extra xp and get on with your life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 12-02-2015, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T09:07:57-08:00","id":778364,"title":"","content":"Honestly, to me, &quot;getting the shaft&quot; is part of the appeal of playing a Ghost Wolf. If I'm makinf a Ghost Wolf character, it's because I want that character to be an underdog. The story of the tribeless lone wolf struggling against adversity and the inherent disadvantages of being a loner in a pack based society is, to me, strengthened by the fact that the character is at a significant disadvantage and gets nothing to compensate for it. If that's not your thing though, I second Amravanti's suggestion of just giving the character some bonus XP if you need something to compensate for the drawbacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T09:55:59-08:00","id":778411,"title":"","content":"I agree with idea that Ghosts Wolves gets freedom. Theme that those who surrenders some of their freedom gets more stuff from the great powers shouldn't be unknown, and in a way it is, or was, a part of the Forsaken and Pure relation to their totems. The only trade-off I could think of lies with the GM who must perhaps make a little point that the oaths of the tribes are not something like a hobby or a general advice for conduct. If you play up this, but not overdo it, then perhaps the freedom of the Ghost Wolf would make more sense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T10:43:57-08:00","id":778449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/778315-why-do-ghost-wolves-get-the-shaft-so-hard?p=778333#post778333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A ghost wolf is <i>literally</i> just &quot;werewolf with no tribe.&quot; What they did is take your standard werewolf character generation, looked at the bit where you add tribe, and then just skipped it. You could then join a tribe in-game, and the renown and gift could just slot into place seamlessly, as if you started like that. I wouldn't charge for them if a player did this.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sure mechanically I think it makes sense, you are making a character sans tribe, so you don't get those free benefits. So they miss out on the benefits of that part of character creation. However it doesn't make sense that a character who had to struggle with those weaknesses wouldn't have some extra skills or something they have learned through their adversity. So I think they should get some merits or skills that show them having survived on the run and alone. <br /> <br /> The game is called Werewolf: The Forsaken. Ghost wolves aren't really Forsaken yet because they don't have first born totems. Ghost wolves are portrayed as characters who haven't gotten with the program yet. I think that it makes for an interesting character and implies you are playing a character whose arc is about holding onto humanity and/or refusing to join the Forsaken properly. So I can see the argument that they are not complete characters and don't need any compensation for their lack tribal bonuses. <br /> <br /> However I think that there are decent Ghost Wolf concepts outside of this idea. As an example if a player wanted to play an &quot;Eater of the Dead&quot;, he should probably get equivalent experience points to what he missed out in character creation. I could also imagine a particularly dangerous kind of Ghost Wolf who associates way too closely with Lunes and is some sort of Lunar Cultist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T11:13:06-08:00","id":778473,"title":"","content":"Ghost Wolves appeal to me a lot, narratively, and I think that lack of mechanical backup helps that. Running a Ghost Wolf (or running a Ghost Wolf game) lets you do something closer to the &quot;wolfman&quot; model, which is a mode I always thought the game lacked in the first edition. The random person who can suddenly turn into a hulking wolf beast, and there's jack shit she can do about it. It works even better now that dramatically failing lunacy can turn you into a Wolf-Blooded, and then maybe a werewolf. Put a whole pack of them together, and you've got a really interesting dynamic. Ghost Wolves let you play up the horror aspect of the werewolf myth. Not that the tribes don't, but Ghost Wolves have that &quot;what have I become?!&quot; quality I occasionally miss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T11:13:17-08:00","id":778474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AForgeForThoughts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/778315-why-do-ghost-wolves-get-the-shaft-so-hard?p=778449#post778449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> However it doesn't make sense that a character who had to struggle with those weaknesses wouldn't have some extra skills or something they have learned through their adversity. So I think they should get some merits or skills that show them having survived on the run and alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>They haven't survived on the run or alone. That's something that happens in-game or as a special part of their background, something any werewolf could have tacked on. If you want your character to have certain skills due to them having a certain background, they have ten merit dots to spend for that. If you feel your character deserves some special abilities because they've had a different life, then that's something you should take up with your storyteller.<br /> <br /> As for benefits, they also don't have a ban.<br /> <br /> When further books come out there might be some expansion on ghost wolf concepts, but since the core book is meant to be about the core experience of the game, which focuses on the five core tribes of the Forsaken and not the Ghost Wolves, Pure or the Bale Hounds or even Lodges, they had no reason to have extra sections tacked on to detract from the core game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-02-2015, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T11:34:41-08:00","id":778485,"title":"","content":"Things you get from a tribe in char gen: Gift affinity. Tribal merits/rites. Dot of Renown. Bonus Shadow gift.<br /> <br /> Gift affinities you get obviously from your association with the tribe and its totem.<br /> Tribe based merits/rites are obviously exclusive.<br /> Dot of renown you earn during your initiation trial.<br /> Gift you receive during the branding, one assumes - Or the elders take you on a hunt to teach you a gift in commemoration of your acceptance.<br /> <br /> The latter two are things that a werewolf <i>could</i> have as a Ghost wolf, but are not an intrinsic part of the creation of one. He is operating alone, without a millenia of tribal knowledge and a network of experienced tribemates and mentors. He is going to be at a disadvantage.<br /> <br /> That's part of the romance of playing the Ghost Wolf, as others have said. You are an underdog. You know the benefits of the system and you said fuck it anyway, I'm my own wolf. If a werewolf cared half as much as the OP does about the disadvantages, he'd have joined a tribe.<br /> <br /> I said before you can throw 3 xp to a player if he really feels disadvantaged, but it's not really necessary and generally doesn't make sense. All things being equal, a ghost wolf doesn't really gain more experience being alone than an uratha in a tribe does. He might have it a little tougher, but he's also missing out on the experience of tribemates. And honestly, he doesn't even really have it tougher when you consider tribal expectations toward prey and purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 12-02-2015, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T13:04:16-08:00","id":778540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/778315-why-do-ghost-wolves-get-the-shaft-so-hard?p=778474#post778474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They haven't survived on the run or alone. That's something that happens in-game or as a special part of their background, something any werewolf could have tacked on. </div> </div> </div> </div>The details of what happened specifically are irrelevant. <br /> <br /> Werewolves in standard character creation are not mechanically brand new werewolves. So there is a backstory of events that happened between being a brand new werewolf and one who has joined a tribe and is a member of pack. The Ghost Wolf most likely goes through something similar, just having made the choice to avoid joining a tribe in the end. <br /> <br /> Ghost Wolves start with an experience deficit. It can be justified from a narrative point of view, but it isn't the only possibility.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/778315-why-do-ghost-wolves-get-the-shaft-so-hard?p=778474#post778474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When further books come out there might be some expansion on ghost wolf concepts, but since the core book is meant to be about the core experience of the game, which focuses on the five core tribes of the Forsaken and not the Ghost Wolves, Pure or the Bale Hounds or even Lodges, they had no reason to have extra sections tacked on to detract from the core game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghost Wolves did get a section in the book, with one of the best pieces of art (IMO). In fact Onyx Path bothered to even make a t-shirt for them. They were mentioned as an important part of the Iraq setting. They have a whole lodge filled with Ghost Wolves.<br /> <br /> I never said the core book needed extras sections. I don't think either groups of Ghost Wolves needed special mechanics, just some light room for further customization in the form of &quot;Here is three experiences have fun!&quot;. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T14:38:43-08:00","id":778603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AForgeForThoughts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/778315-why-do-ghost-wolves-get-the-shaft-so-hard?p=778540#post778540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves in standard character creation are not mechanically brand new werewolves. So there is a backstory of events that happened between being a brand new werewolf and one who has joined a tribe and is a member of pack. The Ghost Wolf most likely goes through something similar, just having made the choice to avoid joining a tribe in the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what character creation is. Your character isn't a baby, whether they've joined a tribe or not, they have merits and skills and specialties because they've existed in some form or another. A Ghost Wolf by default hasn't had a more fulfilling or active life than a Forsaken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ghost Wolves start with an experience deficit. It can be justified from a narrative point of view, but it isn't the only possibility. </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A werewolf gets renown for joining a tribe. When you get renown you get a gift. Ghost Wolves haven't joined a tribe, they don't get that renown, so they don't get that gift. In exchange you aren't bound to a tribal ban and get all those non-mechanical benefits that you wanted for choosing a Ghost Wolf in the first place.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I never said the core book needed extras sections. I don't think either groups of Ghost Wolves needed special mechanics, just some light room for further customization in the form of &quot;Here is three experiences have fun!&quot;. </div> </div> </div>You're choosing to make a character who hasn't had the experience the Forsaken have. I disagree that Ghost Wolves should have a special advantage because they choose not to take advantage of the option to join a tribe. I also disagree that they 'get the shaft' for their decision. I suggested that maybe in later books they'll get more options, as they did in first edition, but I don't see why they should rewrite the already-published core book to offer you an option that you can simply have a Storyteller implement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-02-2015, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T14:45:26-08:00","id":778605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/778315-why-do-ghost-wolves-get-the-shaft-so-hard#post778315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To an extent, I get it. This is a game about being part of a pack, a larger community, and they want to encourage you to be part of that. But if you give me the option not to join a tribe, I'd at least like it to be a viable option. Especially when the book makes a point of saying that just because a guy doesn't join a tribe doesn't mean he's abandoned his duties or doesn't want to be part of the Uratha.<br /> <br /> Ghost Wolves get one less dot of renown than everyone else. They get one less gift. They can't start with the second dot of their moon gift. And for all of this they get... nothing. There's no trade-off. There's no benefit to it. If someone sees Ghost Wolves in the book and decides &quot;That sounds kind of cool, I'd like to try that&quot; then the book essentially slaps them in the face for seeing an option it presents them with an liking it.<br /> <br /> I get that werewolves join tribes for a reason. I get that in a game about being part of something larger than yourself, the guy who's standing off on his own is going to be missing out on something. But when you give me an option to play something in a game, I shouldn't just be punished for picking it.<br /> <br /> For contrast, in Masquerade, if you decided you wanted to play a Caitiff, there were some serious consequences to that, but there were a few fringe benefits. All your disciplines cost the same xp, more than an in-clan discipline, but less than for out-of clan, so you could play around with it. You didn't have a clan weakness, outside of being ostracized in vampire society. It was honestly not as good an option as picking a clan, but you got a few trade-offs for choosing the harder road.<br /> <br /> In Forsaken, you get the shaft.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean, in my games, as a house rule everyone else has to buy at least one dot of tribe status, so only ghost wolves can start with 3 dots of Primal Urge...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T15:39:04-08:00","id":778640,"title":"","content":"It's a tricky issue. I mean, the sentiment behind the sanctity of merits rule is pretty well on the side of someguywithakatana. However, I think I agree with Nofather, it's a tradeoff between that renown dot and a tribal ban. Its not exactly equal, but it's still something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T21:30:04-08:00","id":778798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/778315-why-do-ghost-wolves-get-the-shaft-so-hard?p=778603#post778603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">That's what character creation is. Your character isn't a baby, whether they've joined a tribe or not, they have merits and skills and specialties because they've existed in some form or another. A Ghost Wolf by default hasn't had a more fulfilling or active life than a Forsaken.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">I in no way have argued the conclusion that Ghost Wolves have more fulfilling or active lives up into the start of the story. You restated my point, while the young wolf was doing something to prove himself to the tribe, the Ghost Wolf was doing something else. While the prospective Iron Master was busy showing herself to earn her cunning a Ghost Wolf may have been attempting to struggle with his new nature while attempting to maintain enrollment in college or working in a hospital. </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/778315-why-do-ghost-wolves-get-the-shaft-so-hard?p=778603#post778603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A werewolf gets renown for joining a tribe. When you get renown you get a gift. Ghost Wolves haven't joined a tribe, they don't get that renown, so they don't get that gift. In exchange you aren't bound to a tribal ban and get all those non-mechanical benefits that you wanted for choosing a Ghost Wolf in the first place.</span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">That is hardly equitable. One could easily view the lack of affinity gifts as being enough of an exchange to be without an Oath. Not to mention that the Siskur-Dah condition has no mechanical support for a Ghost Wolf rite master. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">The tribal oaths are mostly narrative devices anyways. </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/778315-why-do-ghost-wolves-get-the-shaft-so-hard?p=778603#post778603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> I suggested that maybe in later books they'll get more options, as they did in first edition, but I don't see why they should rewrite the already-published core book to offer you an option that you can simply have a Storyteller implement.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Rewrite the book? Who is calling for this? </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">This conversation started with criticism. Even then, seeing any call for changes as a call for a rewrite is uncharitable and over the top. If the writers</span><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> wanted to make minor changes to a design decision like &quot;Ghost wolves get three experiences that can't be spent on Renown or Primal Urge&quot; they could be put in a blog post. If they had the time and money to do it maybe a one page pdf. Or they could put something in the open development blogs.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T21:55:12-08:00","id":778804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AForgeForThoughts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/778315-why-do-ghost-wolves-get-the-shaft-so-hard?p=778798#post778798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I in no way have argued the conclusion that Ghost Wolves have more fulfilling or active lives up into the start of the story. You restated my point, while the young wolf was doing something to prove himself to the tribe, the Ghost Wolf was doing something else. While the prospective Iron Master was busy showing herself to earn her cunning a Ghost Wolf may have been attempting to struggle with his new nature while attempting to maintain enrollment in college or working in a hospital.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why they have the same dots to spend on Skills, Attributes and merits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is hardly equitable. One could easily view the lack of affinity gifts as being enough of an exchange to be without an Oath. Not to mention that the Siskur-Dah condition has no mechanical support for a Ghost Wolf rite master. </div> </div> </div>It has no special Condition because they're not a member of a tribe and don't have a favored prey. If you're choosing to not be a member of a tribe, why would you have the same benefits of someone in a tribe? Why not choose to be a member of a tribe to begin with?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rewrite the book? Who is calling for this? </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AForgeForThoughts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/778315-why-do-ghost-wolves-get-the-shaft-so-hard?p=778540#post778540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said the core book needed extras sections. I don't think either groups of Ghost Wolves needed special mechanics, just some light room for further customization in the form of &quot;Here is three experiences have fun!&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This conversation started with criticism. Even then, seeing any call for changes as a call for a rewrite is uncharitable and over the top. If the writers wanted to make minor changes to a design decision like &quot;Ghost wolves get three experiences that can't be spent on Renown or Primal Urge&quot; they could be put in a blog post. If they had the time and money to do it maybe a one page pdf. Or they could put something in the open development blogs. </div> </div> </div>Presumably if they were interested in making these changes they would be in the core book to begin with, as the point was brought up during the open editing period when changes were still being made to the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T22:20:06-08:00","id":778812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/778315-why-do-ghost-wolves-get-the-shaft-so-hard?p=778804#post778804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Which is why they have the same dots to spend on Skills, Attributes and merits.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">No, one werewolf gets a renown, the other does not. According to the table a renown is worth three experience. </span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/778315-why-do-ghost-wolves-get-the-shaft-so-hard?p=778804#post778804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It has no special Condition because they're not a member of a tribe and don't have a favored prey. If you're choosing to not be a member of a tribe, why would you have the same benefits of someone in a tribe? Why not choose to be a member of a tribe to begin with?</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That is irrelevant. The point is that it is something they don't have access to it mechanically. </span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/778315-why-do-ghost-wolves-get-the-shaft-so-hard?p=778804#post778804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Presumably if they were interested in making these changes they would be in the core book to begin with, as the point was brought up during the open editing period when changes were still being made to the book.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This is irrelevant and isn't a reason to dismiss criticism. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Take notice that my quote did not call for a rewrite and used the past tense &quot;needed&quot; so could not have been implied. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T22:32:56-08:00","id":778814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AForgeForThoughts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/778315-why-do-ghost-wolves-get-the-shaft-so-hard?p=778812#post778812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, one werewolf gets a renown, the other does not. According to the table a renown is worth three experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>One werewolf got a renown for joining a tribe, the other didn't join a tribe so didn't get renown.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is irrelevant. The point is that it is something they don't have access to it mechanically. </div> </div> </div>It's perfectly relevant. You don't have access to it because you made a choice not to have access to it. Choosing to be a Ghost Wolf is choosing to miss out on the benefits of being in a tribe, mechanically and narratively.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is irrelevant and isn't a reason to dismiss criticism. </div> </div> </div>As I've said before I don't think Ghost Wolves get the shaft, and I've explained why I've dismissed that criticism. There are plenty of posts here and in the other thread about the matter offering solutions to your issue, but I've made it clear I don't believe Ghost Wolves should get a special bonus at character creation because they reject tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T00:25:59-08:00","id":778837,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's going to be a winning argument in, &quot;A Ghost Wolf's life experiences should be worth more mechanically.&quot; I can easily make a character concept that could be made with less dots than creation allows, or would require more dots than the creation spread allows. Ghost Wolves don't have some universal experience that Tribal Uratha don't. The struggles they deal with are not inherently worth more than the struggles another werewolf deals with joining a Tribe.<br /> <br /> There's also a significant issue with the idea that Ghost Wolves should have a mechanical advantage other werewolves do not. A Ghost Wolf can always join a Tribe, gaining what they didn't get in creation. Unless whatever they would have is lost in the process, they'd actually end up better off than characters just made in a Tribe in first place.<br /> <br /> So, what sort of bonus should they get? If we give them 3XP, and say they get the perks of joining a Tribe for free (including a Renown dot), they're 3 XP up unless they lost 3XP in buying now-favored Gifts. Etc.<br /> <br /> What would be an appropriate advantage that would get lost if they join a Tribe? How does it make sense in-character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T03:12:21-08:00","id":778887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AForgeForThoughts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/778315-why-do-ghost-wolves-get-the-shaft-so-hard?p=778449#post778449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure mechanically I think it makes sense, you are making a character sans tribe, so you don't get those free benefits. So they miss out on the benefits of that part of character creation. <b>However it doesn't make sense that a character who had to struggle with those weaknesses wouldn't have some extra skills or something they have learned through their adversity.</b> So I think they should get some merits or skills that show them having survived on the run and alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. What if, and hear me out, what if... Being a Ghost Wolf normally entails coping out; Denial of your base nature to some extent or another; and maybe, just maybe slacking like a kid who just finished highschool and has no idea what career to follow? That doesn't sounds eligible for &quot;extra skills&quot;, quite the contrary. Tribes, on the other hand, train their initiates. They wouldn't have a sporting chance on their initiations otherwise.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AForgeForThoughts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/778315-why-do-ghost-wolves-get-the-shaft-so-hard?p=778449#post778449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The game is called Werewolf: The Forsaken. Ghost wolves aren't really Forsaken yet because they don't have first born totems.</b> Ghost wolves are portrayed as characters who haven't gotten with the program yet. I think that it makes for an interesting character and implies you are playing a character whose arc is about holding onto humanity and/or refusing to join the Forsaken properly. So I can see the argument that they are not complete characters and don't need any compensation for their lack tribal bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>What color is their brand? Silver-like? Then to the spirit-world at large fucking an Uratha over who hasn't picked a sacred prey is like getting to your prey's young. Yummy, yummy babies. So yeah, in a sense? They're even more Forsaken than the <i>Lushar Iduthag.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T04:15:53-08:00","id":778905,"title":"","content":"It depends on how you look at it. The Pure would likely be a bit more favourable to them because they may still have those nasty silver brands but that's not <i>their</i> fault. They just changed before anyone could shield them from Luna's horrible gaze. So they should just come along and get fixed up with some nice red ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T05:29:13-08:00","id":778930,"title":"","content":"Just calculate what joining a clan would net them experience-wise and give it to them. End of discussion. The book doesn't necessarily say to do that but who cares? Make the argument to your ST and gain the difference. That said, if you join a tribe later, you shouldn't be given anything for free, you should have to spend time, effort, and experience (the time, effort, and experience started werewolves are assumed to have spent) learning these new skills. Simple, right?<br /> <br /> Should these be part of the base rules? Arguably. Are they? No. Is it simple to fix? Seems pretty easy to me as long as you have a reasonable ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 12-03-2015, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T07:06:33-08:00","id":779772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/778315-why-do-ghost-wolves-get-the-shaft-so-hard#post778315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghost Wolves get one less dot of renown than everyone else. They get one less gift. They can't start with the second dot of their moon gift.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually... while the first is correct, the second two are false. Ghost wolves can very much start off with two dots in their Auspice Renown. It would be the only Renown, but its doable. Furthermore, the Character Creation section for Gifts says you choose two Shadow Facets, one Moon Facet, and another Moon or a Wolf Facet. So, even Ghost Wolves end up with 4 Facets. And everyone gets two dots of Rites.<br /> <br /> The only advantages you get for joining a Tribe are the free dot of Renown, access to affinity Gifts, access to a Tribe-exclusive merit and a Rite; easy enough to ignore the extra affinities, given the wealth of other merits, facets, renown, and rites you can purchase. I don't see any specific mechanics tied to the whole Ban, so I'm going to ignore that. In any case, from a purely mechanical perspective, you basically have a 3 EXP difference. That's it.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT - at least in 2e. Are we talking about 1e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T07:15:07-08:00","id":779776,"title":"","content":"No, they're talking 2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gifts: Ghost Wolves have no Gift affinities and start play<br /> with only one Shadow Gift.<br /> Tribal Renown: Ghost Wolves have no Tribal Renown<br /> and cannot start play with their two-dot Moon Gift. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T12:16:40-08:00","id":780026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/778315-why-do-ghost-wolves-get-the-shaft-so-hard?p=779772#post779772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually... while the first is correct, the second two are false. Ghost wolves can very much start off with two dots in their Auspice Renown. It would be the only Renown, but its doable. Furthermore, the Character Creation section for Gifts says you choose two Shadow Facets, one Moon Facet, and another Moon or a Wolf Facet. So, even Ghost Wolves end up with 4 Facets. And everyone gets two dots of Rites.<br /> <br /> The only advantages you get for joining a Tribe are the free dot of Renown, access to affinity Gifts, access to a Tribe-exclusive merit and a Rite; easy enough to ignore the extra affinities, given the wealth of other merits, facets, renown, and rites you can purchase. I don't see any specific mechanics tied to the whole Ban, so I'm going to ignore that. In any case, from a purely mechanical perspective, you basically have a 3 EXP difference. That's it.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT - at least in 2e. Are we talking about 1e?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm talking 2e, and like Elfive said, yeah. The page on ghost wolves says they start with just 1 shadow gift and can't get their 2-dot moon gift. Honestly, that's where I think the overkill is. If it was just that they start with 1 less dot of renown, I think that'd be fair. Having less gifts kind of makes sense, I guess, but it hurts. And I don't see why they shouldn't be able to start with their 2-dot moon gift. It seems like a LOT more shit being thrown on them than is necessary or prudent<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T12:20:00-08:00","id":780033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/778315-why-do-ghost-wolves-get-the-shaft-so-hard?p=778887#post778887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Emphasis mine. What if, and hear me out, what if... Being a Ghost Wolf normally entails coping out; Denial of your base nature to some extent or another; and maybe, just maybe slacking like a kid who just finished highschool and has no idea what career to follow? That doesn't sounds eligible for &quot;extra skills&quot;, quite the contrary. Tribes, on the other hand, train their initiates. They wouldn't have a sporting chance on their initiations otherwise.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What color is their brand? Silver-like? Then to the spirit-world at large fucking an Uratha over who hasn't picked a sacred prey is like getting to your prey's young. Yummy, yummy babies. So yeah, in a sense? They're even more Forsaken than the <i>Lushar Iduthag.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Except being a Ghost Wolf doesn't mean copping out. It says in the book that a lot of ghost wolves are dudes who understand their duty, but who just don't feel they jive with any of the 5 tribes. But even beyond that, they have their moon auspice, and they get a second dot of renown. To me, that suggests that even if they haven't joined a tribe, they've sworn the Oath of the Moon. They're presented in the core forsaken book, because even if they don't jive with the larger culture, they are forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T12:30:32-08:00","id":780044,"title":"","content":"Ghost Wolves are not Forsaken, no. Some Ghost Wolf groups may be heavily aligned with the Forsaken, even seen as Forsaken by some other groups thereof, but it is by no means the default or inherent state of Ghost Wolves.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T12:35:57-08:00","id":780051,"title":"","content":"I figured that from your write-up of Paris and some of the settings, but it should be interesting to see other examples in future books. It's a neat idea, more of a neutral third party than a 'Forsaken, just not part of the Tribes' group. Also gives more reason for characters of all Tribes to be suspicious of them, while letting you play someone who can have goals and ideas wholly independent from the Tribes, or not, if you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T12:42:28-08:00","id":780060,"title":"","content":"Indeed, you have Ghost Wolf groups across the entire scale of allegiance, belief and objectives - Lycaon's Hounds of the Field, the Temple of Apollo, the Eaters of the Dead and more besides. The Lodges rules should help properly empower this element of the game for use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T16:55:40-08:00","id":780232,"title":"","content":"Chris: Again, what color is their renown brands?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T03:07:17-08:00","id":780468,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure it defaults to silver. It's more the &quot;has an auspice&quot; colour than the &quot;forsaken&quot; colour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T04:21:25-08:00","id":780494,"title":"","content":"So, do Ghost Wolves that doesn't take the Oath of the Moon and follow it, keep the same augmented silver Bane like the Pure? Or does it take the utter rejection of Luna by virtue of slicing away the Auspice marks for that to trigger?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T04:39:29-08:00","id":780500,"title":"","content":"Ghost Wolf renown brands are usually silver.<br /> <br /> The augmented silver bane is a result of the ritual the Pure use to flense away the auspice; a Ghost Wolf who has never even heard of the Oath of the Moon only suffers the normal silver band.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T16:42:11-08:00","id":780774,"title":"","content":"I rest my case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T20:10:09-08:00","id":780872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/778315-why-do-ghost-wolves-get-the-shaft-so-hard?p=780774#post780774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I rest my case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your case that Ghost Wolves aren't Pure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T03:26:25-08:00","id":781055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/778315-why-do-ghost-wolves-get-the-shaft-so-hard?p=780872#post780872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your case that Ghost Wolves aren't Pure?</div> </div> </div> </div>Go read the previous page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T06:24:52-08:00","id":781101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AForgeForThoughts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The game is called Werewolf: The Forsaken. Ghost wolves aren't really Forsaken yet because they don't have first born totems</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>to wich Ephsy in response</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What color is their brand? Silver-like? Then to the spirit-world at large fucking an Uratha over who hasn't picked a sacred prey is like getting to your prey's young. Yummy, yummy babies. So yeah, in a sense? They're even more Forsaken than the <i>Lushar Iduthag.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I think Ephsy refers to this, Charlaquin.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T17:39:30-08:00","id":781418,"title":"","content":"It's certainly true that Ghost Wolves can have a hard time of it, but then they haven't shouldered the burdens, duties and spiritual bindings that the Forsaken have.<br /> <br /> The spirit world in <i>gener\u200bal</i> does not consider a Ghost Wolf to be one of the Forsaken, but:<br /> - An individual spirit or group may have a diverging opinion, a grudge or other reason to basically treat <i>Thihirtha Numea</i> like Forsaken.<br /> - A <i>Ghost Wolf</i> can mostly act like a Forsaken through choice or accident.<br /> - A spirit might look at the odds of a given silver-branded werewolf being Forsaken based on what they know of the local werewolf population.<br /> - Plenty of spirits also don't much like the Pure either, so just not necessarily being Forsaken is no protection.<br /> - Some spirits simply don't care or cannot comprehend about <i>any </i>differentiation between werewolves at all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T15:07:58-08:00","id":781865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/778315-why-do-ghost-wolves-get-the-shaft-so-hard?p=781055#post781055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Go read the previous page.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat seems a bit less polite than you probably intended. Just pointing out it reads awkwardly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T15:10:34-08:00","id":781869,"title":"","content":"I've no idea what he meant either, this is the only page I see in this thread has so far.<br /> <br /> Maybe that the Ghost Wolves are seen as 'more' Forsaken than your average tribal member? Or preyed upon more by spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-07-2015, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T16:56:32-08:00","id":781947,"title":"","content":"See my post a little up here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T15:28:11-08:00","id":802383,"title":"","content":"Yeah its tricky to argument by comparing Ghost Wolves to Caitiffs of Masquerade because of the major changes of &quot;political vs. personal horror&quot; between cWoD and nWoD and also character creation mechanics. But I agree with you, so I'll make closer comparisons - Covenants (Vampires) and Orders (Mages). I didn't read much about Changellings, Prometeans and Geists factions but I wouldn't be surprised if they were the same for the sake of this discussion.<br /> <br /> Not belonging to a Covenant or Order, for game mechanics sake, means the character won't have access to new disciplines or halved-cost merits (or new merits if we're talking 2nd Edition). On the story, it means the characters doesn't belong to an organization so they don't have access to them and so they are &quot;less important to less people&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'd say that the social benefits of being on a faction balances the drawbacks (demands) on a quid-pro-quo weight. But then the game offers benefits for the characters belonging to the faction, which are not automatic, but paid by experience (or by using a discipline dot on the convenant power, for example).<br /> <br /> What about Ghost Wolves? If you read both 1st and 2nd editions, they both carry the social stigma from the tribes, which should compensate for the extra liberty (or is it really? not having the tribe's brand on the Hisil may make some antagonists cockier). But the difference between &quot;tribeless uratha&quot; to a factionless vampire or mage is that the later ones doesn't get anything less on their character creation, they only lose options which are primely on character advancement. Not only Ghost Wolves has one less renown dot and begin with one less gift (on both editions) but they also have only their auspice gifts as their affinity gifts (also on both editions), while tribe werewolves would have 2 or 3 more, depending on the auspice-tribe combination.<br /> <br /> The thing is, it makes sense for them to start with one less renown because that comes from joining the tribe and the gift also comes with the renown. But yeah, reading both books makes the concept tempting to a different kind of uratha, who would most-certainly be part of the multi-tribe pack the players are forming, so why should the tribeless one be so weaker?<br /> <br /> To make a way to compensate this and make ghost-wolf characters more playable, we should think about what Ghost-Wolves DO have as advantage, I think their disconnection with the tribes could come in some other benefits. Lets say we give them 3 extra points of merits (1st and second edition), which should be spent in a list of merits. This could be allies (to tribes or lodges) and a ghost wolf could even have contact or allies with The Pure, acting as a double-agent for even as an ambassador, given their disconnection with the tribe war. Status and Resources can make sense if you think that the uratha choosed to mantain his former &quot;mortal&quot; life and focus on it the best he could instead of adapting his ways and adress to best fit in the tribe (and think about having to leave work to fulfill tribe's demands/necessities). Totem merit can justify a ghost-wolf uratha devoted to his pack above all tribes. The list can go on - a lot of merits make sense.<br /> <br /> Even still, I'd say that, in the long run, a tribe uratha character would still evolve stronger than a tribeless one, but this way they would at least feel less &quot;naked&quot;. Another way would also make the merits of this list cost half price for Ghost Wolves - much like tribe/order/covenant benefit - but only allow this discount for buying 1 dot and 2 dot merits (1st Edition). Beyond that would be too much to explain based on the benefits of being tribeless and that would also make it balanced somehow. On 2nd Edition, I'd say you could give the ghost wolf a 1-point experience discount upon unlocking non-affinity shadow gifts, to incentive versality (note that it's still expensive and it would still make them cost more than affinity gifts, which tribe uratha has access from a lot).<br /> <br /> Almost off-topic:<br /> <br /> I started a WtF - Second Edition campaing with four players and named it &quot;The Ghost Wolves&quot; (we played two long sessions so far). Only one of my players had played WtF before (and not much) and the idea was to storytell the First Change and then an experienced NPC Ghost Wolf gathered them one by one and taught them all of the basics and the deal was that he'd present them to the Tribes of Moon on a much bigger city (they were on a medium one with no werewolf society) already &quot;cooked and ready&quot; (in enchange of favors from whatever tribe would accept each). But then NPC dies misteriously (killed) just when they were ready to travel and this severs any connection they might get to the Tribes. So the campaing is about ghost wolves who made their city their territory, and their personal lives their major concern. Since the players know little-to-nothing about Wereweolf, I want them to enjoy the personal horror and supernatural aspects of being a half-fleshed-shapeshifting-spirit-walker-self-aware-monster, without the extra layer of the politics of Uratha. I personaly like each of the five tribes, but I feel like playing with already-shifted characters and already in a tribe would be best for players who already has some experience with the scenario. I'm using the house rule I just stated above for the players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10798,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10798-kitsune-sensei","user":"Kitsune Sensei","date":". 01-06-2016, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10798-kitsune-sensei","name":"Kitsune Sensei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10798_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T15:57:44-08:00","id":802403,"title":"","content":"The problem with comparing them to other game lines... is that you just stopped with vampires. Vampires get the least creation stuff from their social splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}